Job Summary:

PsiQuantum is seeking a Senior Operations Planning Analyst to own the recurring supply, demand, and capacity planning cycle for a complex manufacturing environment. This role will maintain planning data and models, reconcile inputs across systems, track supplier and component commitments, identify emerging constraints, and prepare clear weekly analysis and recommendations for management review.
The analyst will help leaders make timely, well-informed decisions by providing a reliable view of demand, supply, labor capacity, production availability, and risk. The role is central to improving execution, surfacing constraints earlier, and reducing dependence on a single individual for critical planning activities. It will partner closely with operations, manufacturing, engineering, finance, IT, suppliers, and systems teams.
This role owns the operational planning process, planning models, data quality, requirements, and decision support. Management retains accountability for capacity strategy, major supply and production tradeoffs, executive escalations, planning governance, and recovery decisions.

